<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n483" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăchĕlōĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pertaining to the river Achelous</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 16, 265</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Callirrhoë,</span>”
				<i>daughter of Achelous</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					9, 413</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Aetolian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">heros,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Tydeus</i>, <i>the son of Oeneus</i>,
						<i>king of Aetolia</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 142</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
